 ## Background
-StyleRF-VolVis is the first work in VolVis that targets style transfer in the NeRF space [S1]. It builds on NeRF representation  and Instant-NGP architecture . It adapts NeRF's palette-based recoloring strategy  and uses Knowledge Distillation (KD)  to transfer color knowledge. It differs from prior works like ARF  and SNeRF  by supporting both photorealistic and non-photorealistic editing in a single framework and preserving view-dependent lighting [S1].
+StyleRF-VolVis is the first work in VolVis that targets style transfer in the NeRF space [S1]. It builds on NeRF representation and Instant-NGP architecture [S1]. It adapts NeRF's palette-based recoloring strategy and uses Knowledge Distillation (KD) to transfer color knowledge [S1]. It differs from prior works like ARF and SNeRF by supporting both photorealistic and non-photorealistic editing in a single framework and preserving view-dependent lighting [S1].
 
